uct or service now  these situations  only exist inside consumers these are  not something you can you can give to  them  it's something that's a build up over  time if you  as a brand operator are consistent with  your brand experience  so we can ask ourselves what do we need  to build a brand  and my experience from mcdonald's was  that mcdonald's  was found to be one of the largest  brands in the world  but we realized when i was working there  that no one had brand  on their name card no one had the name  brand as part of their job function  so we said how can we become one of the  world's largest brands  if known specifically in charge of brand  and what we realized was that we had  basically over decades  been maniacally focused with consistency  around standards that we had set  ourselves so over time  people came to rely on mcdonald's for  very particular experience  so in my mind everything you need to do  to build a brand is to set your own  standards  and be consistent with these over time  every store  of the customer and your brand and the  brand experience  will automatically come from that  now why are brands then important well  customers and consumers like value they  like to get as much as they can  for as little as possible so i find this  equation where we say  brand experience over price is the value  you provide to your customers  so you can say either you cut prices and  therefore the value goes up  or you can grow the brand experience and  therefore the value will go up and my  talk of course is about really about the  brand experience design  um that we can we can hopefully all  learn something from  so what we know about brands are that  they do take time and they do require  resources  people and money to be built but they  also provide momentum  in times of trouble whether you have a  temporary crisis it may be food  poisoning or whether you are seeing  something like what we expected right  now  kobe 19 brands haven't mentioned that  carry you  through these so it makes sense for us  to invest in building brands  secondly brands are a great way to  capture and defend  sales markets here and profit because  once you have occupied a space  with consumers once you have taken the  time and resources to enter  consumers minds and create these  associations you sit there  and other market entrants will have a  struggle to come in and compete with you  perfect example is that that four  figures success  created a lot of market entrance but  most of them failed because they were  really much more in the area of  executing providing people some chicken  rather than creating a brand experience  and then lastly brands  create economic value and i will show an  example of what i mean with that  so let's take a cup of coffee as an  example  if you go out and you buy some beans you  need about 10 grams of beans to make a  cup of coffee  that is a commodity if you take  ground beans from a pack then you are  using a product  if you go to the kopitian and you buy a  cup of coffee  you're getting a service and if you go  to starbucks  you are getting a brand experience  now the amount of coffee needed for  these four examples  is the same but if you look at what  happens on how much money people spend  if you buy copper beans as a commodity  you spend a few cents  you spend a bit more once it becomes a  product  when it's a service competition 1.50  but if you go to starbucks you spend a  lot more than that  but the input costs are more or less the  same the cost of the coffee beans  is more or less the same in all these  examples but by building a brand  experience  starbucks create immense value around  those coffee beans  now i will introduce the term customer  journey which to me  really is sort of what happens when  someone sees your brand for the first  time  and when will they eventually after  having tried you decide whether to come  back  or not um i used to go to chicago quite  a lot when i work with mcdo